  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transparent policy making: Caribbean Cooperative MRV Hub (CCMRVH)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Measurement, Reporting &amp; Verification (MRV)/transparency is an important foundation for domestic policy-making and essential for meeting new tracking and reporting requirements under the framework of the Paris Agreement. Many small island developing states (SIDS) at high risk from climate change have limited budgets, insufficient national expertise, and small staff size leading to inefficient MRV systems and an over-reliance on outside experts. The Caribbean Cooperative Measurement Reporting &amp; Verification Hub (CCMRVH) functions as a country-driven institution staffed with regional experts and dedicated to building capacity across the Caribbean through training and dissemination of regionally appropriate tools and guidance documents. The project helped Caribbean states design, establish, and run in-house MRV systems, capable of gathering and processing data, creating greenhouse gas inventories, modeling climate mitigation measures, and tracking progress towards national climate targets.</narrative>
  </description>
